WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.520
At some point, every great series must come
to an end.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.740
Sometimes you get a satisfying coda to a wonderful
experience, and sometimes that eagerly-anticipated

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.210
series finale turns out to be the loogie that
ruins the punchbowl.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.740
As much as we all love The Walking Dead, it
can't go on forever.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.940
When the walkers finally stop walking, how
do we think it'll all go down?

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.240
The walkers evolve

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.180
We don't really know much about zombie biology,
but we do know about viruses.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.710
Viruses evolve, sometimes because of environmental
factors, and sometimes against human intervention.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:40.000
Right now, the zombies are shambling, hungry
monsters who hunt based on smell and sound,

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.530
but what if they're capable of... becoming
more?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.510
Zombies are strong, but they're slow, and
can only really use two senses.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:52.120
The virus and the human body seem to have
a symbiotic relationship after death.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.070
So there's nothing really stopping the virus
from mutating these guys into a whole new

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.620
kind of zombie.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.399
Virus mutation is not altogether unlikely,
and when that happens, mankind is totally

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:03.719
toast.

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:04.719
The walkers win

00:01:04.719 --> 00:01:08.090
There are simply far more walkers on Earth
than there are living people.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:12.720
And even though humans possess superior intelligence,
they just can't seem to keep it together as

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.710
well as the brainless dead can.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:18.460
Humans lack unity, and zombies have an amazing
persistence.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.490
As we watch the last struggling group of survivors
dwindle, in a world gone wild from neglect,

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.840
they’ll eventually run out of resources.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.360
The food options suck…

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:32.560
“Peanut butter and jelly, diet soda and
pigs feet.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:35.760
That’s a white trash brunch right there.”

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:39.770
...and no one seems to really pursue farming
too seriously.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:44.899
It's a pathetic, whimpering death…but it's
depressingly closer to reality than any apocalypse

00:01:44.899 --> 00:01:47.539
we've ever seen before on TV.

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:50.759
If The Walking Dead is one thing, it's depressing.

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:51.819
The humans win

00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:56.260
We know almost nothing about walker physiology,
other than the fact that their guts make a

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:57.479
great disguise.

00:01:57.479 --> 00:02:01.389
“Oh this is bad, it’s really bad.”

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:06.429
They die when their brains are injured, and
they spread a zombie-making disease, but that's

00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:07.590
really about it.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:11.810
At this point, we haven't met a single zombie
that's died of natural causes, so we can only

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.450
assume that they're basically immortal if
unharmed.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:19.420
But walkers are also easily killed with just
about anything pointy and well-aimed.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:23.360
It's been suggested that the walkers are the
Earth's answer to environmental changes.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.171
So if humans stop acting stupid and focus
on cleansing the world of the undead, the

00:02:28.171 --> 00:02:31.080
planet's ecology will be better off than ever.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.140
Zombies make amazing mulch.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:36.200
It might not be great for the surviving humans
who have a hankering for pizzas rolls, but

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.660
you can't please everyone.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:42.790
Cremation becomes mandatory, and mankind crawls
back to the top of the food chain.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.600
Utopia is discovered

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.350
Between The Walking Dead and Fear the Walking
Dead, we’ve only really seen what’s happening

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.430
on the coasts.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.650
We have no idea what's happening in the middle
states, aside from some hints from a network

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.650
of park rangers.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.810
We also don’t have any idea about what's
happening in the rest of the world.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:03.260
We've seen maybe 2% of what's really going
on out there, which leaves a lot to the imagination.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:06.950
Once we know that Rick’s party is truly
safe, we'll be able to sleep at night, and

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.400
the series can end.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.700
On Marc Maron's WTF podcast, creator Robert
Kirkman said he'd like to see the TV series

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:18.280
end on a positive note, so real, actual, measurable
success isn't out of the question.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.430
A cure is found

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:24.500
Disease experts are in pretty short supply,
but we've seen labs and hospitals as sanctuaries.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:28.280
While it seems unlikely that someone will
whip up a zombie cure and crop-dust the entire

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:32.240
planet with it, the discovery of something
to counteract the zombie virus would pretty

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.240
much save the world.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.480
No, it won't restore Grandpa to normal, but
at least it'll stop him from hungering for

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.520
living flesh, which is a pretty fair compromise.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.620
It ends with Rick

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:46.220
When a show loses its star, it rarely lasts
more than a couple of seasons before totally

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.260
collapsing.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:51.300
Rick is really the compass of the group, even
when he's spinning wildly off course.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:55.290
While characters like Daryl and Carol are
interesting to watch evolve, The Walking Dead

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.790
is Rick's story from beginning to end, and
without him, we just don't have a focal point.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:04.600
Whether Rick just can't survive the thousandth
onslaught, he manages to pass from old age,

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:09.430
or Andrew Lincoln just decides that it's time
to go, Rick's story is the only story.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:13.790
Like a canary in a coalmine, once Rick is
gone, start preparing for the bitter end.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.030
Then again, Carl's story is also a part of
Rick's story.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:21.120
We'd only like to see Rick dying in a final
episode sort of deal, where he passes the

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:26.229
torch of leadership to the guy who was by
his side throughout the entire zombie apocalypse,

00:04:26.229 --> 00:04:27.939
his son.

00:04:27.939 --> 00:04:29.840
Thanks for watching!

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.669
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:33.669 --> 00:04:37.009
And leave us a comment to let us know how
you think The Walking Dead will end...

